      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\sin(x+30^\\circ)$ using $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$.\n\n$\\sin(x+30^\\circ)=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the sum formula for sine:\n$$\n\\sin(u+v)=\\sin u\\cos v+\\cos u\\sin v.\n$$\nApply it and substitute the exact special-angle values:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin(x+30^\\circ)&=\\sin x\\cos 30^\\circ+\\cos x\\sin 30^\\circ\\\\\n&=\\sin x\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)+\\cos x\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\sin x+\\frac{1}{2}\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
